/-!
# Preadmissible generation for semiample dlt threefolds

Let `(X_i, B_i)`, `i ∈ I`, be a finite collection of `ℚ`-factorial projective dlt pairs on complex
threefolds whose adjoints `D_i = K_{X_i} + B_i` are semiample. Every component of the reduced floor
`⌊B_i⌋` is a normal surface `S_P` carrying its adjunction pair `(S_P, B_{S_P})`. Then there is
`m₀ > 0` with the following property. Let `m > 0` be divisible by `m₀`, and suppose the admissible
section systems on the finite collection of all floor components of all `X_i` (systems compatible
under every crepant birational map between floor components and between their strata) generate
every `𝒪_{S_P}(m(K_{S_P} + B_{S_P}))`. Then for every finite set `T` of such admissible floor
systems there is `q > 0` such that in degree `qm` the preadmissible section systems on the
collection `(X_i, B_i)` (compatible under all crepant maps between proper strata) generate every
`𝒪_{X_i}(qmD_i)`, and the `q`-th power of every system of `T` is the system of Poincaré residues of
some preadmissible system.

## Main results

* `MMP.Fourfold.exists_generatesOn_and_isPoincareResidue_pow_of_mem_admissibleSections`:
  preadmissible generation and lifting of powers of admissible floor systems.

## Implementation notes

The floor components are indexed by pairs `(i, P)` with `P` a prime divisor of `X_i` and
`⌊coeff_P B_i⌋ ≠ 0`; for each such pair the surface `S_{i,P}`, a closed immersion
`j_{i,P} : S_{i,P} ⟶ X_i` onto `P` and the different `B_{S_{i,P}}` form an adjunction step
(`MMP.Fourfold.IsAdjunctionStep`); since floor components of a dlt pair are normal, `S_{i,P}` is
the normalization of `P`. Admissibility on the floors is `MMP.Fourfold.admissibleSections` of a
residue restriction structure on this collection of surface pairs; preadmissibility on the
threefolds is `MMP.Fourfold.preadmissibleSections`. Generation of the restricted adjoint on the
non-normal floor is read on its normal components: on a proper surjective model a section is
nonvanishing at a point if and only if its pull-back is nonvanishing at any preimage.
The `q`-th power of a floor section `t = f · ω^{⊗m}`, `ω` a rational top form, is
`f^q · ω^{⊗qm}` (`MMP.Fourfold.formPow`).

## References

* [J. Kollár et al., *Flips and abundance for algebraic threefolds*][KollarFlips]
-/

