/-- **Preadmissible generation for semiample dlt threefolds.** Let `(X_i, B_i)`, `i ∈ I` finite, be
`ℚ`-factorial projective dlt pairs (`MMP.Fourfold.IsPair`, `MMP.Intersection.IsDltPair`) on complex
threefolds with canonical divisors `K_i` such that `K_i + B_i` is semiample. For every prime
divisor `P` of `X_i` with `⌊coeff_P B_i⌋ ≠ 0` let `j_{i,P} : S_{i,P} ⟶ X_i` with the divisor
`B_{S_{i,P}}` be the adjunction step onto `P`. Then there is `m₀ > 0` such that for every positive
`m` divisible by `m₀` residue restriction structures in degree `m` exist on the collection of all
floor pairs `(S_{i,P}, B_{S_{i,P}})`, and for every such structure `Rf` whose admissible systems
generate every `𝒪_{S_{i,P}}(m(K + B_{S_{i,P}}))` at every point, and for every finite set `T` of
admissible floor systems, there is `q > 0` such that residue restriction structures on the
collection `(X_i, B_i)` in degree `qm` exist, and for every such structure `R`:
* at every point of every `X_i` some preadmissible system `s ∈ preadmissibleSections R` has its
  `i`-th section generating `𝒪_{X_i}(qm(K_i + B_i))` on a neighbourhood of the point;
* for every `t ∈ T` some preadmissible system `s` has, along every `j_{i,P}`, the Poincaré residue
  of `s_i` equal to `t_{i,P}^q`: if `t_{i,P} = f · ω^{⊗m}` then the residue is `f^q · ω^{⊗qm}`. -/
@[mmp "thm_fourfold_semiample_dlt_preadmissible_generation"]
public theorem exists_generatesOn_and_isPoincareResidue_pow_of_mem_admissibleSections
    {I : Type*} [Finite I] {X : I → Scheme.{0}} [∀ i, IsIntegral (X i)]
    [∀ i, IsLocallyNoetherian (X i)] [∀ i, IsNormal (X i)]
    {sX : ∀ i, X i ⟶ Spec (.of ℂ)} (hX : ∀ i, Mori.IsProjectiveVariety ℂ (sX i))
    (hdim : ∀ i, topologicalKrullDim (X i) = 3) (hQ : ∀ i, IsQFactorial (sX i))
    {B : ∀ i, QDivisor (X i)} (hB : ∀ i, IsPair (sX i) (B i))
    (hdlt : ∀ i, MMP.Intersection.IsDltPair (sX i) (B i)) {K : ∀ i, Divisor (X i)}
    (hK : ∀ i, (K i).IsCanonicalDivisor (sX i) 3)
    (hsemi : ∀ i, QDivisor.IsRelativelySemiample (sX i) (Divisor.toQDivisor (K i) + B i))
    (Sf : (Σ i, {P : Mori.PrimeDivisor (X i) // ⌊(B i).coeff P⌋ ≠ 0}) → Scheme.{0})
    [∀ j, IsIntegral (Sf j)] [∀ j, IsLocallyNoetherian (Sf j)] [∀ j, IsNormal (Sf j)]
    (jf : ∀ j, Sf j ⟶ X j.1) (BSf : ∀ j, QDivisor (Sf j))
    (hSf : ∀ j, IsAdjunctionStep (sX j.1) (B j.1) (jf j) (BSf j) ∧
      Set.range (jf j).base = (j.2.1.support : Set (X j.1))) :
    ∃ m₀ : ℕ, 0 < m₀ ∧ ∀ m : ℕ, 0 < m → m₀ ∣ m →
      Nonempty (ResidueRestriction (fun j => jf j ≫ sX j.1) BSf 2 m) ∧
      ∀ Rf : ResidueRestriction (fun j => jf j ≫ sX j.1) BSf 2 m,
        (∀ j (y : Sf j), ∃ t ∈ admissibleSections Rf, ∃ V : (Sf j).Opens, y ∈ V ∧
          GeneratesOn (BSf j) m V
            ((t j : logPluricanonicalSections (jf j ≫ sX j.1) 2 m (BSf j)) :
              RationalPluriForms (jf j ≫ sX j.1) 2 m)) →
        ∀ T : Finset (∀ j, logPluricanonicalSections (jf j ≫ sX j.1) 2 m (BSf j)),
